</Description>
<Members>
<Member Name="OperatingMode" DataType="SINT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Determines the drive operating mode when “Start Motion” has a zero-to-one transition (1 - Position mode; 2 - Speed mode; 3 - Home mode; 4 - Torque mode; 5 - Gear mode; 6 - Index mode)]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="Control1" DataType="SINT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write"/>
<Member Name="ServoOn" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="Control1" BitNumber="0" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A zero-to-one transition will servo on the drive.]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="ServoOff" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="Control1" BitNumber="1" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A zero-to-one transition will servo off the drive.]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="StopMotion" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="Control1" BitNumber="2" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A zero-to-one transition will stop the drive.]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="FaultReset" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="Control1" BitNumber="3" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A zero-to-one transition will try to clear the fault of the drive.]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="StartMotion" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="Control1" BitNumber="4" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A zero-to-one transition means the motion command is issued from the external controller.]]>
</Description>
</Member>
