<EncodedData EncodedType="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="raC_Dvc_K5100_MAM" Class="Standard" Revision="1.1" RevisionExtension=".01" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" EditedDate="2019-09-03T05:55:02.945Z" SoftwareRevision="v32.00" EncryptionConfig="9">
<Description>
<![CDATA[K5100 (2198-Exxxx-ERS) - Use the Motion Axis Move (MAM) instruction to move an axis to a specified position.]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[September 2019, initial release.]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[============================================================
Instruction Overview:
-----
K5100 (2198-Exxxx-ERS) - Use the Motion Axis Move (MAM) instruction to move an axis to a specified position.


Supplemental Descriptions:
-----
Sts_ERR codes:(Value - Description)
100 – Drive is not ready.
101 – Drive is faulted.
103 – MSF is executing.
105 – Drive is disabled.
107 – MAS is executing.
108 – Other motion AOI is sending the command.
111 – SpeedReference is out of range.
112 – AccelReference is out of range.
113 – DecelReference is out of range.
117 – NonCyclicMoveType is out of range.
118 – CyclicMoveType is out of range.
119 – TravelMode is either 2 or 10.
126 – Homing is not completed.
127 – Previous motion has not completed.
129 – Motor is not connected.


Revision Notes:
-----
1.1.01
- September 2019, initial release.


=============================================================== 

Disclaimer of Warranty
